<!--
  RUT_SealedSleeper.xml                  UtinniPatches · COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  Resolves ledger slug
  `the_cracked_lands:sealed-signature-sleeper-wax-lined-burrow-water-wake-
  sheds-c` (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_cracked_lands.md §10 "The
  Sealed": "creatures that sleep through the dry years. They survive the
  way Earth's lungfish does — sealed inside a wax-lined burrow under the
  cracked clay, metabolism banked to almost nothing, until water wakes them
  ... The Farmers read them as living dowsing rods ... Their shed
  burrow-lining is crack-wax (§11)."; rosters/the_cracked_lands.json
  new_defs row 2, mechanic_load "C#: water-trigger wake + crack-wax
  product; borrow the dormant comp (107-row family)").

  Checked cast_assignment.csv first, per this item's own "watch out":
  RUT_CrackedLands.xml's wildAnimals block already tags TWO existing
  species against the-Sealed SORT — `RSW_MutagenicNorphea` ("the-Sealed,
  keep") and `AA_SandSquid` ("the-Sealed, adjust-keep"). Those fill the
  bestiary SORT (dormant-fauna category); neither is the roster's own
  requested SIGNATURE species carrying the specific wax-lined-burrow/
  water-wake/crack-wax mechanic — same "sort-filler vs. flagship" gap
  RUT_MortuaryCrawler's own header worked through for AA_Helixien one
  biome over. Both stay exactly as-is; this is a new fourth species, not a
  replacement.

  🔴 THE NAME IS NOT SETTLED. `RUT_SealedSleeper` is the INTERNAL working
  defName; "the Sealed" in the sheet names the GROUP/sort (same shape as
  "the Mortuary Guild"/"the Spenders"/"the Patient"), not a ruled species
  label for the individual creature — same posture RUT_MortuaryCrawler's
  own header used. Folded into a new owner card,
  `CRACKEDLANDS_SHIPPING_NAMES_1` (filed this pass; no existing
  the_cracked_lands naming-draft doc was found the way poison_forest/
  scarlands/propane_lakes/miasma each had one).

  MECHANISM, and what genuinely could not be built inline: the dormancy
  itself is stock (`CompCanBeDormant`/`CompWakeUpDormant`, RimWorld/
  CompWakeUpDormant.cs read in full this pass) — but that comp's only wake
  triggers are `wakeUpOnDamage`, `wakeUpOnThingConstructedRadius`, and
  `wakeUpIfAnyTargetClose` (a TargetingParameters check, default
  `ForColonist()`; no water/terrain-type targeting exists in the stock
  class). There is no stock "wakes when water reaches it" trigger, exactly
  what the roster's own mechanic_load flags. Shipped here as an INTERIM
  stand-in, same "stands in with plain elevated aggression until it
  lands" posture PROPANE_LAKE_PIPE_MECHANICS_1's RUT_VWake used:
  `wakeUpOnDamage=true` (something disturbs the burrow) and
  `wakeUpOnThingConstructedRadius=6` (a Farmer building a cistern/vaporator
  square on top of a dowsing-rod cluster wakes it — a plausible reading of
  "the Farmers read them as living dowsing rods," even though it is a
  construction trigger, not the sheet's own water-arrival trigger). The
  genuinely-new piece — a small rare-tick comp that activates
  CompWakeUpDormant when a nearby cell turns to real (non-boil) water
  terrain, plus the "gather crack-wax off the flats after a wake" job —
  is filed as its own dedicated item, `CRACKED_LANDS_SEALED_WAKE_MECHANISM_1`,
  rather than guessed at inline (this item's own precedent for a
  genuinely-new-C#, non-trivial piece: PYRELANDS_BURROWER_GRAZER_1,
  MIASMA_KARRATHIL_POLLINATION_GATE_1). `receivesSignals=true` is set per
  `CompProperties_CanBeDormant.ConfigErrors` (RimWorld/
  CompProperties_CanBeDormant.cs, read this pass) — required whenever
  `jobDormancy` is false, which it is here (a wild dormant state, not an
  activity-driven one).

  Crack-wax: wired as an interim `butcherProducts` yield (RUT_CrackWax,
  this item's own companion file, RUT_CrackedLandsItems.xml) rather than
  the sheet's actual "gathered off the flats after a wake" ground-drop —
  that drop-on-wake behaviour is part of the same deferred mechanism item
  above.

  Body: `QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail`, same body RUT_MortuaryCrawler
  (this item, the_scarlands wave) used for a squat, digging, armored
  scavenger-adjacent species — a reasonable "lungfish analog with legs"
  silhouette for a burrower, not a literal fish body (no aquatic BodyDef
  fits "sealed inside a burrow under cracked clay").

  Art: genuinely new, no existing render found (checked infrastructure/
  artpipe/{done,pending,registry.jsonl} for "sealed"/"sleeper"/"dowsing" —
  clean, only unrelated hits). Three facing jobs filed this pass
  (south/east/north; west mirrors east) — rutsealedsleeper_v1_{south,east,
  north}.json.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RUT_SealedSleeper</defName>
    <label>Sealed sleeper</label>
    <description>A squat, armor-clad burrower that spends almost its whole life motionless under the cracked clay, banked down inside a wax-lined burrow the way Earth's lungfish rides out a dry year. Walk the famous cracked-pan flats and you are walking on sleeping animals — the Farmers read where they cluster thickest as the surest sign of water underfoot, and prize the pale wax it sheds when it finally wakes.</description>
    <receivesSignals>true</receivesSignals>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.6</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>32</Mass>
      <MarketValue>90</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.35</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>0</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>68</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.15</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>digging claws</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>5</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>digging claws</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>5</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_CanBeDormant">
        <startsDormant>true</startsDormant>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_WakeUpDormant">
        <!-- INTERIM triggers, see header: no stock water-arrival trigger
             exists. wakeUpOnThingConstructedRadius INVENTED at 6 (a
             Farmer's cistern/vaporator built directly over a dowsing
             cluster). -->
        <wakeUpOnDamage>true</wakeUpOnDamage>
        <wakeUpOnThingConstructedRadius>6</wakeUpOnThingConstructedRadius>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <baseBodySize>0.7</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.9</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.15</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Heavy</leatherDef>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <roamMtbDays>25</roamMtbDays>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>30</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>14</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.5, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(1.5, 0.5)</li>
          <li>(2, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.25</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.6</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Herbivore_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <butcherProducts>
      <RUT_CrackWax>2</RUT_CrackWax>
    </butcherProducts>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RUT_SealedSleeper</defName>
    <label>Sealed sleeper</label>
    <race>RUT_SealedSleeper</race>
    <combatPower>18</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1~1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.4</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_SealedSleeper/RUT_SealedSleeper</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
